From 5b13a986b7d448dffb6f32e3c790bf0e761c78d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:27:05 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Allocation form: departments enter lecturers, units and
 groups, and download it

Units and groups now come from the Timetable Generator (its
/api/integrations/allocator endpoints, GENERATOR_API_KEY), so departments
fill in their allocation where the Director's office entered the timetable.

- Each department keeps its own lecturer list (title, name, staff number,
  FT/PT, phone, email, weekly hour limit); one person on two lists is
  recognised by staff number.
- The form: per unit or group, a lecturer and L/P/CF hours. Servicing
  classes are marked; units not in the timetable can be typed in and are
  flagged. Once the timetable is published, lecturer clashes and weekly
  hour limits are refused.
- Paste from Excel/Word (lecturers are added from "Dr. Name (PT)"),
  COD submit/reopen, and a Directorate progress view.
- Downloads as PDF, Word and Excel in the allocation form layout.
- Migration 0003, tests with a fake Generator, new frontend pages.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UKcxXFW2Czwg9FhZjJfLy3
